      "verdict": "SUPPORTED (for the subset of cases it chooses to decide)",
      "explanation": "Among the 55/168 cases the engine auto-decided (32.7% coverage), FNR=0.0303 - substantially better than XGBoost alone (FNR=0.2581). BUT the ALL-CASE real-output FNR (counting deferred cases as not-flagged, matching what the system actually surfaces to a user today) is 0.6559 - worse than either raw model. The engine improves decision quality only where it is confident enough to commit; it does not improve the system's current end-to-end FNR as actually surfaced, because so much is deferred."
    },
    "H4": {
